.TH QUAKESTRIKEPH-TOOLKIT 8 "22 November 2026" "QuakeStrikePH" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
quakestrikeph-toolkit \- provision, restore, remove, and rebuild the QuakeStrikePH demo
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sudo bash quakestrikeph-accounts.sh
[\-\-directory PATH]
.PP
.B sudo bash quakestrikeph-config.sh
[\-\-output FILE] [\-\-directory PATH]
.PP
.B sudo bash quakestrikeph-install.sh
\-\-archive FILE \-\-config FILE [\-\-directory PATH]
.PP
.B sudo bash quakestrikeph-restore.sh
\-\-backup FILE [\-\-directory PATH]
.PP
.B sudo bash quakestrikeph-uninstall.sh
[\-\-directory PATH] [\-\-confirm]
.PP
.B sudo bash quakestrikeph-rebuild.sh
\-\-archive FILE \-\-backup FILE [\-\-config FILE] [\-\-directory PATH]
.PP
Every script also accepts
.B \-\-help
without root privileges.
.SH DESCRIPTION
These six Bash scripts implement IT 123 Option 1C (Provision and Rebuild) for the
QuakeStrikePH web application (Bulletin, Backend, PostgreSQL, and Redis).
They target Ubuntu 24.04 LTS and Debian 13 with systemd and support offline
deployment using cached APT packages and two prepared archives:
.B quakestrikeph-app.tar.gz
(application source, model artifacts, and exported Docker images) and
.B quakestrikeph-db-backup.sql.gz
(compressed PostgreSQL backup containing public/test earthquake and forecast data only).
.PP
The default installation folder is /srv/quakestrikeph and the Docker Compose
project name is quakestrikeph-sam. Every script is safe to run twice without
duplicating accounts, rotating existing credentials, or wiping existing database records.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B quakestrikeph-accounts.sh
Creates or reuses the locked service user and group
.B quakestrikeph
(UID/GID 10001, no login shell, no sudo or Docker access) and applies least-privilege
permissions to the application folder (750 for directories and scripts, 640 for
ordinary files, 600 root-only for .env).
.TP
.B quakestrikeph-config.sh
Generates a private root-only .env file (mode 600) with four random OpenSSL
passwords and matching database URLs. If the output file already exists, it is
kept unchanged; if output is missing and an installed .env exists, it is copied
to keep database credentials in sync.
.TP
.B quakestrikeph-install.sh
Validates inputs, installs Docker offline from the local APT cache, loads
images.tar, copies application files and .env into /srv/quakestrikeph, runs
database role creation, migrations, and model registration, starts Backend and
Bulletin, and verifies both HTTP responses.
.TP
.B quakestrikeph-restore.sh
Checks gzip integrity of the supplied .sql.gz backup, skips restore if earthquake
records already exist, streams the backup into PostgreSQL, refreshes role grants,
and confirms records were loaded.
.TP
.B quakestrikeph-uninstall.sh
Previews removal of quakestrikeph-sam containers, volumes, networks, application
files, and the quakestrikeph service account by default. Passing
.B \-\-confirm
performs the deletion while keeping Docker, cached images, backups, and external
configuration files intact.
.TP
.B quakestrikeph-rebuild.sh
Checks disk space with df, verifies both compressed archives, runs accounts,
config, install, final permissions, and database restore in order, and verifies
Backend and Bulletin HTTP responses.
.SH EXAMPLES
Full offline rebuild on a blank server:
.nf
sudo bash quakestrikeph-rebuild.sh \e
    \-\-archive /root/quakestrikeph-app.tar.gz \e
    \-\-backup /root/quakestrikeph-db-backup.sql.gz
.fi
.PP
Run the individual scripts in order:
.nf
sudo bash quakestrikeph-accounts.sh
sudo bash quakestrikeph-config.sh \-\-output /root/demo.env
sudo bash quakestrikeph-install.sh \e
    \-\-archive /root/quakestrikeph-app.tar.gz \e
    \-\-config /root/demo.env
sudo bash quakestrikeph-accounts.sh
sudo bash quakestrikeph-restore.sh \e
    \-\-backup /root/quakestrikeph-db-backup.sql.gz
.fi
.PP
Preview clean uninstall (safe, deletes nothing):
.nf
sudo bash quakestrikeph-uninstall.sh
.fi
.PP
Perform confirmed clean uninstall:
.nf
sudo bash quakestrikeph-uninstall.sh \-\-confirm
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /root/demo.env
Private external configuration file (mode 600, root-owned). Keep outside Git.
.TP
.B /srv/quakestrikeph/
Default application installation directory.
.TP
.B /srv/quakestrikeph/.env
Installed root-only configuration file (mode 600).
.TP
.B /srv/quakestrikeph/infrastructure/compose.checkoff.yml
Compose override generated during installation.
.TP
.B /var/cache/apt/archives/
Cached APT packages used for offline Docker installation.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Command succeeded, help output was printed, or uninstall preview completed.
.TP
.B 1
A validation check or deployment step failed. Check the error message on stderr.
